--- !u!114 &912010398
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 912010396}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d03038af81819cd46b24eff87a25452b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OXQuizManager
  row:
    oTile: {fileID: 60076108}
    xTile: {fileID: 1754096119}
  questions:
  - questionText: Adults produce over 1 liter of saliva every day.
    correctAnswerIsO: 1
    explanationText: Adults produce about 1 to 1.5 liters of saliva each day.
  - questionText: Different parts of the tongue can only taste certain flavors.
    correctAnswerIsO: 0
    explanationText: All parts of the tongue can detect all basic tastes.
  - questionText: Tongue patterns are different for each person.
    correctAnswerIsO: 1
    explanationText: The surface patterns of the tongue are unique enough to be studied
      for biometric technology.
  - questionText: Lips do not have sweat glands like normal skin.
    correctAnswerIsO: 1
    explanationText: Lips dry out easily because they do not have sweat or oil glands.
  - questionText: People often become better at eating bitter foods as they get older.
    correctAnswerIsO: 1
    explanationText: This happens because of changes in taste and repeated food experiences.
  - questionText: The longest human tooth recorded in Guinness World Records was
      over 4 cm long.
    correctAnswerIsO: 0
    explanationText: The longest recorded human canine tooth was about 3.67 cm long.
  - questionText: There are billions of bacteria living inside the mouth.
    correctAnswerIsO: 1
    explanationText: Even after brushing, many bacteria still remain inside the mouth.
  - questionText: People produce much more saliva while sleeping.
    correctAnswerIsO: 0
    explanationText: Saliva production almost stops during sleep, which can cause
      bad breath in the morning.
  - questionText: The tongue can get tired.
    correctAnswerIsO: 1
    explanationText: The tongue is made of muscles, so it can become fatigued after
      heavy use.
  - questionText: Teeth have a different structure from bones.
    correctAnswerIsO: 1
    explanationText: Unlike bones, teeth cannot fully repair themselves.
  - questionText: 'Human lips look red because they contain a lot of red pigment. '
    correctAnswerIsO: 0
    explanationText: Lips are thin, so the color of blood vessels underneath can
      be seen through the skin.
  - questionText: The tongue is one of the fastest-healing parts of the body.
    correctAnswerIsO: 1
    explanationText: The tongue heals quickly because it has strong blood flow and
      fast cell repair.
  questionsPerRun: 5
  answerTimeLimit: 5
  correctAnswerDelay: 3
  wrongDamage: 1
  playerOverlapLayers:
    serializedVersion: 2
    m_Bits: 896
  barrierDoor: {fileID: 0}
  OnQuestionReady:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  OnTimerTick:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  OnCorrectAnswer:
